WEBVTT

00:00:01.268 --> 00:00:18.300
Everybody at the Grierson Art Gallery in Los Angeles was very excited.

00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:37.522
George Grierson, the boss, stood outside the gallery and looked at the people in front of him.

00:00:37.582 --> 00:00:41.494
He smiled and turned to the cameras.

00:00:41.554 --> 00:00:51.198
This is a great day for the Grierson Gallery and a great day for America, he said.

00:00:51.258 --> 00:00:58.838
In two weeks, the most famous painting by an American artist is coming back home.

00:00:58.898 --> 00:01:01.156
Yes, everybody.

00:01:01.216 --> 00:01:09.410
America's most wonderful painting, Whistler's Mother, will be here in my gallery.

00:01:09.470 --> 00:01:15.762
At the National Gallery in London, everybody was very excited too.

00:01:15.822 --> 00:01:22.668
The Grierson Gallery wanted somebody from London to go to America for two months.

00:01:22.728 --> 00:01:32.973
They wanted a top man from the National Gallery to talk to people about the artist Whistler and his famous painting of his mother.

00:01:33.033 --> 00:01:36.354
Who was the right person for the job?

00:01:36.414 --> 00:01:41.286
Dr. Rosenblum or Dr. Cutler?

00:01:41.346 --> 00:01:47.608
At a meeting in one of the rooms in the gallery, everybody wanted to go.

00:01:47.668 --> 00:01:52.583
But first, they had to discuss a more important problem.

00:01:52.642 --> 00:01:54.686
Mr. Bean.

00:01:54.746 --> 00:01:58.548
Nobody in the room liked Mr. Bean.

00:01:58.608 --> 00:02:01.700
They all wanted him to leave the gallery.

00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:02.970
Why?

00:02:03.030 --> 00:02:04.942
What was wrong with the man?

00:02:05.002 --> 00:02:11.124
He only had to sit in one of the rooms in the gallery all day and watch the paintings.

00:02:11.184 --> 00:02:14.196
He wasn't very good at his job.

00:02:14.256 --> 00:02:16.678
He usually fell asleep.

00:02:16.737 --> 00:02:20.573
But why did they all hate him?

00:02:20.633 --> 00:02:29.149
Suddenly, the National Gallery's boss, Mr Walton, came into the room and sat down at the table.

00:02:29.209 --> 00:02:36.389
We're talking about that strange man, Mr Bean, sir, somebody said.

00:02:36.449 --> 00:02:39.940
We all think, be quiet!"

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:42.482
shouted Mr. Walton angrily.

00:02:42.541 --> 00:02:46.214
There's nothing wrong with Mr. Bean.

00:02:46.274 --> 00:02:54.630
He's a wonderful young man, one of the best men in the gallery.

00:02:54.690 --> 00:02:59.612
Nobody in the room said a word.

00:02:59.672 --> 00:03:02.472
They all looked very unhappy.

00:03:02.532 --> 00:03:05.060
Wait a minute!

00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:07.561
Somebody suddenly shouted.

00:03:07.621 --> 00:03:09.582
Of course!

00:03:09.642 --> 00:03:15.835
Why don't we send Mr Bean to the Grierson Gallery in America?

00:03:15.894 --> 00:03:18.276
Nobody spoke.

00:03:18.336 --> 00:03:21.358
It was a stupid idea.

00:03:21.418 --> 00:03:26.670
Or was it Mr Bean in America?

00:03:26.730 --> 00:03:30.102
Two long months without the man.

00:03:30.162 --> 00:03:33.196
Yes, yes, they all shouted.

00:03:33.256 --> 00:03:36.008
That's a great idea.

00:03:36.068 --> 00:03:39.350
Mr. Walton looked very happy.

00:03:39.410 --> 00:03:42.293
Right, don't sit there.

00:03:42.352 --> 00:03:46.245
Get Mr. Bean quickly.

00:03:46.305 --> 00:03:51.319
Mr. Bean sat and waited outside the room.

00:03:51.379 --> 00:03:56.062
Why did these important people want to see him?

00:03:56.122 --> 00:04:00.044
Suddenly he sneezed loudly.

00:04:00.104 --> 00:04:05.166
He took out a paper handkerchief and blew his nose.

00:04:05.226 --> 00:04:08.368
Then he blew it again.

00:04:08.428 --> 00:04:16.504
Then again, more loudly, the noisiest nose blow in the world.

00:04:16.564 --> 00:04:21.818
Mr. Walton called Mr. Bean into the room.

00:04:21.878 --> 00:04:26.381
When he walked in, he smiled at everybody.

00:04:26.441 --> 00:04:34.900
They all looked at him and started laughing Mr. Bean looked very stupid.

00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:41.172
Excuse me, Mr. Bean, Mr. Walton said.

00:04:41.232 --> 00:04:46.855
Something's coming out of your nose.

00:04:46.914 --> 00:04:50.487
It was some of his paper handkerchief.

00:04:50.546 --> 00:04:52.988
It looked very funny.

00:04:53.048 --> 00:04:59.321
Mr. Bean's face went red, and he quickly pulled the paper out of his nose.

00:04:59.381 --> 00:05:01.902
No, Mr. Bean.

00:05:01.962 --> 00:05:04.643
We want to ask you something.

00:05:04.703 --> 00:05:09.234
It's important and very exciting.

00:05:09.294 --> 00:05:15.316
Would you like to go to America?

00:05:15.376 --> 00:05:32.870
Chapter 2 An accident on the plane With the bag in one hand and a big smile on his face Mr. Bean hit it hard.

00:05:32.930 --> 00:05:35.141
Bang!

00:05:35.200 --> 00:05:38.961
America!

00:05:39.021 --> 00:05:42.032
shouted Mr. Bean at the airport.

00:05:42.092 --> 00:05:47.494
I'm going to America!

00:05:47.554 --> 00:05:54.492
With a big smile on his face, he got on the plane and took out his camera.

00:05:54.552 --> 00:06:02.990
This was the beginning of his holiday and he wanted to take photos of everybody and everything.

00:06:03.050 --> 00:06:08.343
He found his seat next to another man, Mr. Tucker.

00:06:08.402 --> 00:06:13.395
Mr. Bean sat down and took a photo of him too.

00:06:13.454 --> 00:06:19.576
Mr. Tucker stopped reading his newspaper and looked at him angrily.

00:06:19.636 --> 00:06:25.164
Then he stood up and quickly moved to the seat in front of him.

00:06:25.224 --> 00:06:32.912
He didn't like strange people, and Mr Bean was very strange.

00:06:32.972 --> 00:06:37.994
Happy in his new seat, Mr Tucker fell asleep.

00:06:38.054 --> 00:06:42.116
Behind him, Mr Bean couldn't sleep.

00:06:42.176 --> 00:06:44.927
He was too excited.

00:06:44.986 --> 00:06:51.593
He smiled at a woman with a young boy, but she didn't smile at him.

00:06:51.653 --> 00:06:55.099
My son's feeling sick, she said.

00:06:55.159 --> 00:06:56.920
How dare!

00:06:56.980 --> 00:06:58.602
said Mr. Bean.

00:06:58.662 --> 00:07:03.916
He was happy, and he wanted other people to be happy too.

00:07:03.976 --> 00:07:10.970
When the boy looked across at him, Mr. Bean took the last sweet from a bag.

00:07:11.030 --> 00:07:17.175
He threw it into the air and caught it in his mouth.

00:07:17.235 --> 00:07:21.018
Did the boy think it was clever?

00:07:21.078 --> 00:07:22.812
No.

00:07:22.871 --> 00:07:26.324
Did the boy laugh or smile?

00:07:26.384 --> 00:07:28.275
He did not.

00:07:28.335 --> 00:07:32.386
He looked strangely at Mr Bean.

00:07:32.446 --> 00:07:35.787
Mr Bean thought for a minute.

00:07:35.847 --> 00:07:42.688
Then he put the sweet bag up to his mouth and began to blow into it.

00:07:42.748 --> 00:07:49.870
He wanted to blow air into the bag and then break it with a loud noise.

00:07:49.930 --> 00:07:51.547
Bang!

00:07:51.607 --> 00:07:54.846
Everybody laughs at that.

00:07:54.906 --> 00:08:00.880
But there was something wrong with the bag and the air got out again.

00:08:00.940 --> 00:08:06.605
The boy's face was grey now and he felt very sick.

00:08:06.664 --> 00:08:12.158
Then he saw a white paper bag in the back of the seat in front of him.

00:08:12.218 --> 00:08:15.745
He took it out and opened it.

00:08:15.805 --> 00:08:18.280
Mr Bean watched him.

00:08:18.340 --> 00:08:20.551
His eyes opened wide.

00:08:20.611 --> 00:08:25.263
Yes, yes, that bag was okay.

00:08:25.323 --> 00:08:28.064
He turned away and laughed.

00:08:28.124 --> 00:08:30.474
He's a clever boy.

00:08:30.534 --> 00:08:36.686
He remembered the bag in the back of the suit, he thought.

00:08:36.746 --> 00:08:42.245
But Mr Bean looked away at the wrong time.

00:08:42.305 --> 00:08:48.534
The boy opened the bag quickly and was sick into it.

00:08:48.594 --> 00:08:52.166
Mr. Bean didn't see him.

00:08:52.226 --> 00:08:58.149
A minute later, before the boy could stop him, Mr. Bean took the bag.

00:08:58.209 --> 00:09:00.890
He quickly blew into it.

00:09:00.950 --> 00:09:04.722
Then he put it in front of Mr. Tucker's face.

00:09:04.782 --> 00:09:14.139
With the bag in one hand and a big smile on his face, Mr. Bean hit it hard.

00:09:14.199 --> 00:09:20.494
Mr. Tucker was not a happy man.

00:09:20.554 --> 00:09:25.835
Some time later, the plane arrived in Los Angeles.

00:09:25.895 --> 00:09:30.156
Mr. Bean looked at the people in the airport.

00:09:30.216 --> 00:09:32.836
I'm in America.

00:09:32.896 --> 00:09:37.018
He thought, this is wonderful.

00:09:37.078 --> 00:09:40.682
He started taking photos again.

00:09:40.742 --> 00:09:44.706
Near a wall, there were two policemen.

00:09:44.766 --> 00:09:50.900
Mr Bean watched them, and then he saw their guns.

00:09:50.960 --> 00:09:55.612
He thought of a game and smiled.

00:09:55.672 --> 00:10:02.706
He put one hand slowly inside his jacket and looked for his gun.

00:10:02.766 --> 00:10:04.596
Not really.

00:10:04.656 --> 00:10:07.678
Mr Bean didn't have a gun, of course.

00:10:07.738 --> 00:10:10.835
He only wanted to play a game.

00:10:10.895 --> 00:10:15.695
The two policemen suddenly turned and saw him.

00:10:15.755 --> 00:10:21.280
They stopped talking and looked carefully at Mr. Bean.

00:10:21.340 --> 00:10:25.214
What was this little man's game?

00:10:25.274 --> 00:10:28.036
Did he have a gun?

00:10:28.096 --> 00:10:29.828
Quick!

00:10:29.888 --> 00:10:31.750
Said one of the policemen.

00:10:31.810 --> 00:10:33.392
He's got a gun!

00:10:33.412 --> 00:10:35.325
Get him!

00:10:35.385 --> 00:10:38.598
Mr. Bean gave them a smile.

00:10:38.658 --> 00:10:42.990
Then he turned and ran the other way fast.

00:10:43.050 --> 00:10:47.180
Everybody on the floor, no!

00:10:47.240 --> 00:10:49.461
shouted the policeman.

00:10:49.521 --> 00:10:52.892
Everybody in the airport was afraid.

00:10:52.952 --> 00:10:55.742
People fell to the ground.

00:10:55.802 --> 00:11:00.594
Mr. Bean saw them and fell to the ground too.

00:11:00.654 --> 00:11:03.544
Not you, stupid.

00:11:03.604 --> 00:11:05.696
A man next to him said.

00:11:05.756 --> 00:11:08.118
How, thank you!"

00:11:08.178 --> 00:11:09.649
said Mr. Bean.

00:11:09.709 --> 00:11:13.612
He got up and started to run away again.

00:11:13.672 --> 00:11:18.244
But the policeman ran faster and caught him.

00:11:18.304 --> 00:11:22.706
They stood in front of him with their guns in his face.

00:11:22.767 --> 00:11:27.950
Slowly, take out your gun, they told him.

00:11:28.010 --> 00:11:32.996
Put it on the floor and stand back.

00:11:33.056 --> 00:11:36.981
Mr. Bean was very afraid.

00:11:37.041 --> 00:11:44.016
He carefully put his hand in his jacket and took out his two fingers.

00:11:44.076 --> 00:11:48.278
It was only a game, he said.

00:11:48.338 --> 00:11:51.921
I haven't really got a gun.

00:11:51.981 --> 00:11:55.012
The policeman looked at him.

00:11:55.072 --> 00:11:58.756
Who was this strange little man?

00:11:58.815 --> 00:12:01.157
Get out of here!

00:12:01.217 --> 00:12:03.441
They shouted angrily.

00:12:03.501 --> 00:12:09.026
Mr. Bean got out fast.

00:12:09.086 --> 00:12:19.398
Chapter 3 Wet trousers He saw a fan.

00:12:19.458 --> 00:12:21.079
Ah!

00:12:21.139 --> 00:12:26.130
He got up and moved slowly across the room.

00:12:26.190 --> 00:12:32.386
Then he started dancing in front of the fan.

00:12:32.446 --> 00:12:37.142
The Langleys were usually a very happy family.

00:12:37.202 --> 00:12:40.964
They lived in a large house in Los Angeles.

00:12:41.024 --> 00:12:45.908
David Langley had an important job at the Grierson Gallery.

00:12:45.969 --> 00:12:50.911
His wife, Alison, was a friendly, intelligent woman.

00:12:50.972 --> 00:13:01.320
They had two lovely children, a 15-year-old daughter, Jennifer, and a seven-year-old son, Kevin.

00:13:01.380 --> 00:13:10.832
One day, David came home from the gallery and said to his family, listen, I've got a great idea.

00:13:10.892 --> 00:13:16.277
A top man from the National Gallery in London is coming to Los Angeles.

00:13:16.337 --> 00:13:18.570
I'd like to invite him here.

00:13:18.630 --> 00:13:21.888
He can stay with us for two months.

00:13:21.948 --> 00:13:26.137
David's family didn't like the idea very much.

00:13:26.197 --> 00:13:28.488
Who was this man?

00:13:28.548 --> 00:13:30.990
A boring Englishman?

00:13:31.050 --> 00:13:33.001
No, thank you.

00:13:33.061 --> 00:13:42.976
Here, in our house, for two months, Alison said, no, David, he can stay in a hotel.

00:13:43.036 --> 00:13:45.476
I'd like it."

00:13:45.536 --> 00:13:47.466
David answered angrily.

00:13:47.526 --> 00:13:50.527
He's a very intelligent man.

00:13:50.587 --> 00:13:53.628
It'll be good for all of us.

00:13:53.688 --> 00:14:00.610
So, Alice and Langley and the children waited for the Englishman's visit.

00:14:00.670 --> 00:14:03.671
The big day arrived.

00:14:03.731 --> 00:14:08.312
Mr. Bean was late, problems with the police at the airport.

00:14:08.372 --> 00:14:12.540
But now he was here in the Langley's sitting room.

00:14:12.600 --> 00:14:16.078
They all looked at him and smiled.

00:14:16.138 --> 00:14:19.379
He didn't look very intelligent.

00:14:19.439 --> 00:14:22.260
He looked very strange.

00:14:22.320 --> 00:14:25.200
Was there something wrong with him?

00:14:25.260 --> 00:14:30.272
Perhaps he was tired after the long journey from England.

00:14:30.332 --> 00:14:35.954
The next morning, David took Mr. Bean to the Grierson Gallery.

00:14:36.014 --> 00:14:43.230
My boss, Mr. Grierson, would like to meet you at 9 o'clock, he told Mr. Bean in the car.

00:14:43.290 --> 00:14:48.898
and he gets angry when people are late, Dr Bean.

00:14:48.958 --> 00:14:54.624
Mr Bean sat in the car and looked out of the window.

00:14:54.684 --> 00:15:00.780
Why did David call him, Dr Bean, not Mr Bean?

00:15:00.840 --> 00:15:08.036
Dr was the name for the top men in the National Gallery, Dr Rosenblum and Dr Cutler.

00:15:08.096 --> 00:15:12.836
They were very intelligent and knew a lot about art.

00:15:12.896 --> 00:15:15.846
He didn't know anything about art.

00:15:15.906 --> 00:15:21.868
But he felt very important when David called him, Dr. Bean.

00:15:21.928 --> 00:15:27.339
When they got to the gallery, Mr. Bean wanted to go to the toilet.

00:15:27.399 --> 00:15:30.039
David looked at his watch.

00:15:30.099 --> 00:15:33.590
The men's room is over there, Dr. Bean.

00:15:33.650 --> 00:15:36.851
But please, don't be too long.

00:15:36.911 --> 00:15:39.929
Mr. Grierson's waiting.

00:15:39.989 --> 00:15:43.628
Mr. Bean walked into the men's room.

00:15:43.688 --> 00:15:48.312
He went to the toilet, and then started to wash his hands.

00:15:48.372 --> 00:15:54.585
But the water went everywhere, over the front of his trousers.

00:15:54.645 --> 00:15:56.866
Oh, no!

00:15:56.926 --> 00:16:00.358
He thought, what am I going to do?

00:16:00.418 --> 00:16:05.132
I can't meet Mr. Grierson with wet trousers.

00:16:05.192 --> 00:16:08.697
Then he saw a machine on the wall.

00:16:08.757 --> 00:16:10.842
Ah, good!

00:16:10.902 --> 00:16:13.584
A hand dryer, he thought.

00:16:13.644 --> 00:16:17.428
That'll dry them in no time.

00:16:17.488 --> 00:16:23.522
Mr Bean jumped up and down, but the machine was too high.

00:16:23.582 --> 00:16:27.663
The warm air didn't blow onto his trousers.

00:16:27.723 --> 00:16:30.902
Then he had an idea.

00:16:30.962 --> 00:16:39.319
He climbed onto a chair in front of the machine and started to move slowly from left to right.

00:16:39.379 --> 00:16:45.254
The warm air blew onto his trousers in the right place.

00:16:45.314 --> 00:16:50.498
Suddenly a man came out of one of the toilets.

00:16:50.558 --> 00:16:53.912
He looked up and saw Mr Bean.

00:16:53.972 --> 00:16:58.270
Then he walked out as fast as possible.

00:16:58.329 --> 00:17:04.196
David Langley stood outside the men's room and waited for Mr. Bean.

00:17:04.256 --> 00:17:06.237
He looked at his watch.

00:17:06.297 --> 00:17:08.608
It was after nine o'clock.

00:17:08.668 --> 00:17:12.840
Dr. Bean, we're late, he shouted.

00:17:12.900 --> 00:17:16.900
Mr. Grierson will be very angry.

00:17:16.961 --> 00:17:21.942
Mr. Bean came out of the men's room and followed David.

00:17:22.002 --> 00:17:24.073
This wasn't funny.

00:17:24.133 --> 00:17:26.585
His trousers weren't dry.

00:17:26.646 --> 00:17:30.298
He wanted more time in front of the hand dryer.

00:17:30.358 --> 00:17:35.509
He couldn't go into Mr Grierson's office with wet trousers.

00:17:35.569 --> 00:17:39.480
Then he saw a newspaper on a table.

00:17:39.540 --> 00:17:46.180
He took the paper and put it in front of his trousers.

00:17:46.240 --> 00:17:51.975
Mr Grierson's office was a beautiful room.

00:17:52.035 --> 00:18:00.662
There were paintings everywhere, and on the wall behind the desk was a big poster of Whistler's mother.

00:18:00.722 --> 00:18:04.694
There were a lot of important people in the room.

00:18:04.754 --> 00:18:08.336
Mr. Grisson looked at his watch.

00:18:08.396 --> 00:18:11.718
Ah, David, good morning!

00:18:11.779 --> 00:18:16.301
And this is our famous Dr. Bean from England.

00:18:16.361 --> 00:18:18.756
How are you, Dr. Bean?

00:18:18.816 --> 00:18:21.982
Mr. Bean said hello to everybody in the room.

00:18:22.042 --> 00:18:24.524
Now, sit down, Dr. Bean!

00:18:24.584 --> 00:18:29.458
said Mr. Grisson, and took the newspaper out of his hands.

00:18:29.518 --> 00:18:32.981
Mr. Bean sat down quickly.

00:18:33.040 --> 00:18:37.594
He didn't want these important people to see his wet trousers.

00:18:37.654 --> 00:18:41.978
Everybody sat round the table, and the meeting began.

00:18:42.038 --> 00:18:45.510
But Mr. Bean didn't listen to a word.

00:18:45.570 --> 00:18:48.676
He couldn't stop thinking about his trousers.

00:18:48.736 --> 00:18:51.302
What could he do?

00:18:51.362 --> 00:18:53.543
He saw a fan.

00:18:53.563 --> 00:18:55.755
Ha!

00:18:55.815 --> 00:19:00.438
He got up and moved slowly across the room.

00:19:00.499 --> 00:19:04.812
Then he started dancing in front of the fan.

00:19:04.872 --> 00:19:09.546
Everybody in the room stopped talking and looked at him.

00:19:09.606 --> 00:19:14.110
What is the man doing, they thought?

00:19:14.170 --> 00:19:17.532
Mr. Bean looked down at his trousers.

00:19:17.592 --> 00:19:20.544
Good, they were dry.

00:19:20.604 --> 00:19:24.039
He turned round and smiled at everybody.

00:19:24.099 --> 00:19:27.473
Then he walked slowly back to his seat.

00:19:27.534 --> 00:19:32.050
He wanted them to see the front of his lovely dry trousers.

00:19:32.110 --> 00:19:35.894
Yes, right.

00:19:35.954 --> 00:19:40.006
Dr. Bean, said Mr. Grisson.

00:19:40.066 --> 00:19:42.218
Please sit down.

00:19:42.278 --> 00:19:49.342
Now, when Whistler's mother arrives at the gallery, we want you to say something.

00:19:49.402 --> 00:19:52.233
About twenty minutes will be fine.

00:19:52.293 --> 00:19:57.506
You know, talk about the artist and his work, okay?

00:19:57.567 --> 00:20:01.418
Mr. Bean didn't understand him.

00:20:01.478 --> 00:20:03.140
Say something.

00:20:03.200 --> 00:20:07.028
But he didn't know anything about art.

00:20:07.088 --> 00:20:12.458
Yes, of course, he said.

00:20:12.518 --> 00:20:16.832
The meeting ended and everybody stood up.

00:20:16.892 --> 00:20:20.525
Mr. Grisson talked quietly to David.

00:20:20.585 --> 00:20:24.138
This, Dr. Bean, David.

00:20:24.198 --> 00:20:28.164
He's the National Gallery's top man, right?

00:20:28.224 --> 00:20:30.069
That's right, sir.

00:20:30.129 --> 00:20:31.430
David answered.

00:20:31.490 --> 00:20:32.962
Good.

00:20:33.022 --> 00:20:39.006
This painting, Whistler's mother, is very important to the gallery.

00:20:39.066 --> 00:20:40.538
You know that.

00:20:40.598 --> 00:20:44.550
I don't want anything to go wrong.

00:20:44.610 --> 00:20:47.894
Do you understand me, David?

00:20:47.954 --> 00:20:50.165
I understand, sir.

00:20:50.225 --> 00:20:51.736
Said David.

00:20:51.797 --> 00:20:58.966
He smiled at his boss, but he didn't feel very happy.

00:20:59.026 --> 00:21:05.914
Chapter 4, at the fairground.

00:21:05.974 --> 00:21:11.296
He sat down and started to work on the computers.

00:21:11.356 --> 00:21:17.768
The ride will be really dangerous now, he laughed.

00:21:17.828 --> 00:21:22.900
That evening David came home and walked into the kitchen.

00:21:22.960 --> 00:21:27.541
Hi Allie, he said, and put his arm around his wife.

00:21:27.601 --> 00:21:30.231
Hi, and said Alison.

00:21:30.292 --> 00:21:35.033
She looked behind David carefully, and then smiled.

00:21:35.093 --> 00:21:36.804
Oh, good.

00:21:36.864 --> 00:21:38.845
No, Dr. Bean.

00:21:38.905 --> 00:21:43.077
I didn't like having that man in our house, dear.

00:21:43.137 --> 00:21:47.639
He isn't here now, but I'm sorry, dear.

00:21:47.699 --> 00:21:50.510
He's coming, said David.

00:21:50.570 --> 00:21:51.852
What?

00:21:51.912 --> 00:21:54.062
Jennifer, Kevin!

00:21:54.122 --> 00:21:55.423
Alison shouted.

00:21:55.483 --> 00:21:57.573
It's Plan B.

00:21:57.633 --> 00:22:00.523
What's Plan B, Allie?

00:22:00.583 --> 00:22:01.904
asked David.

00:22:01.964 --> 00:22:05.546
Plan B is this, David, Alison said.

00:22:05.606 --> 00:22:10.668
The children and I are not going to stay in the same house as Dr. Bean.

00:22:10.728 --> 00:22:12.809
He's too strange.

00:22:12.869 --> 00:22:15.040
He makes funny faces.

00:22:15.100 --> 00:22:19.502
He throws sweets up in the air and catches them in his mouth.

00:22:19.562 --> 00:22:21.953
He broke my best picture.

00:22:22.013 --> 00:22:25.155
He's a very dangerous little man.

00:22:25.215 --> 00:22:28.396
We're going to my mother's for the weekend.

00:22:28.456 --> 00:22:31.558
But Ali, wait a minute!"

00:22:31.618 --> 00:22:33.208
David cried.

00:22:33.268 --> 00:22:35.190
But he was too late.

00:22:35.250 --> 00:22:38.772
Alison and the two children were in her car.

00:22:38.832 --> 00:22:41.584
He watched them drive away.

00:22:41.644 --> 00:22:43.595
Oh, no!

00:22:43.655 --> 00:22:44.646
He thought.

00:22:44.706 --> 00:22:51.950
Dr. Bean will be here all weekend, and I'll have no help from anybody.

00:22:52.010 --> 00:22:58.165
The next day was Saturday, and Mr. Bean wanted to see Los Angeles.

00:22:58.225 --> 00:23:02.548
When he got into David's car, he took out his camera.

00:23:02.608 --> 00:23:04.410
Great!

00:23:04.470 --> 00:23:06.312
He shouted excitedly.

00:23:06.372 --> 00:23:09.463
I'm going to enjoy today.

00:23:09.524 --> 00:23:15.958
David drove through the city, and Mr Bean took photos of everything and everybody.

00:23:16.018 --> 00:23:22.032
People, buildings, policemen, dogs, trees, flowers.

00:23:22.092 --> 00:23:24.200
He was very busy.

00:23:24.260 --> 00:23:30.140
Then he put the camera up in front of David's face and took some photos of him too.

00:23:30.200 --> 00:23:32.762
"'Stop that,' shouted David.

00:23:32.782 --> 00:23:34.512
"'It's dangerous.

00:23:34.572 --> 00:23:37.074
I'm trying to drive.'"

00:23:37.134 --> 00:23:43.048
In the afternoon, they stopped at a fairground in Santa Monica near Los Angeles.

00:23:43.108 --> 00:23:47.890
There were rides and sweet shops and people in funny hats.

00:23:47.950 --> 00:23:51.956
Mr. Bean bought an ice cream and a hat.

00:23:52.016 --> 00:23:55.301
Oh, this is wonderful.

00:23:55.361 --> 00:23:59.074
He shouted and he took more and more photos.

00:23:59.134 --> 00:24:04.708
Look David, that ride says really dangerous.

00:24:04.768 --> 00:24:08.240
Let's go on that.

00:24:08.300 --> 00:24:12.733
The ride was very exciting.

00:24:12.793 --> 00:24:15.715
It went up and down very fast.

00:24:15.775 --> 00:24:18.367
Everybody cried and shouted.

00:24:18.427 --> 00:24:20.646
David was afraid.

00:24:20.706 --> 00:24:24.066
That wasn't really dangerous.

00:24:24.126 --> 00:24:29.097
It was really boring, Mr Bean said at the end.

00:24:29.157 --> 00:24:33.028
They left the ride and walked past the machine room.

00:24:33.088 --> 00:24:39.270
Mr Bean saw the computers and machines in the room and had an idea.

00:24:39.330 --> 00:24:44.301
David, let's go on that ride again, he said.

00:24:44.361 --> 00:24:47.226
Go and buy some more tickets.

00:24:47.286 --> 00:24:50.561
Okay, said David unhappily.

00:24:50.621 --> 00:24:53.572
He felt sick and wanted to go home.

00:24:53.632 --> 00:24:56.822
Mr. Bean walked into the machine room.

00:24:56.882 --> 00:24:58.513
Good.

00:24:58.573 --> 00:25:00.443
Nobody there.

00:25:00.503 --> 00:25:05.364
He sat down and started to work on the computers.

00:25:05.424 --> 00:25:11.574
The ride will be really dangerous now, he laughed.

00:25:11.634 --> 00:25:18.147
Some minutes later, David and Mr Bean were in their seats again, ready for the same ride.

00:25:18.207 --> 00:25:22.190
And this time everybody was really afraid.

00:25:22.250 --> 00:25:25.102
People flew out of their seats into the air.

00:25:25.162 --> 00:25:28.424
But Mr Bean enjoyed every minute of it.

00:25:28.484 --> 00:25:31.876
When they got off the ride, he looked at David.

00:25:31.936 --> 00:25:34.488
David's face was green.

00:25:34.548 --> 00:25:36.990
That was great!

00:25:37.050 --> 00:25:38.281
laughed Mr Bean.

00:25:38.341 --> 00:25:42.032
Those computers are much better now.

00:25:42.092 --> 00:25:46.013
but he didn't see the policeman behind him.

00:25:46.073 --> 00:25:51.846
Later that afternoon in the police station, Mr. Bean stopped laughing.

00:25:51.906 --> 00:25:57.470
What did you do to those computers, you stupid little man?

00:25:57.530 --> 00:26:02.072
The policeman shouted, you hurt a lot of people.

00:26:02.132 --> 00:26:06.366
Mr. Bean looked down at the floor and said nothing.

00:26:06.426 --> 00:26:10.283
The policeman walked angrily out of the room.

00:26:10.343 --> 00:26:14.582
Mr Bean looked up and saw a mirror.

00:26:14.642 --> 00:26:18.544
He stood up and started dancing in front of it.

00:26:18.604 --> 00:26:21.076
Then he made funny faces.

00:26:21.136 --> 00:26:23.728
But it was a two-way mirror.

00:26:23.788 --> 00:26:30.292
In the next room, the policeman and David stood behind the mirror and watched Mr Bean.

00:26:30.352 --> 00:26:35.046
You say he's a top man from the National Gallery in London?

00:26:35.106 --> 00:26:36.856
asked the policeman.

00:26:36.916 --> 00:26:40.177
I, yes, said David.

00:26:40.237 --> 00:26:43.508
And he's very intelligent?

00:26:43.568 --> 00:26:50.924
Yes, he doesn't look very intelligent to me, said the policeman.

00:26:50.984 --> 00:26:54.067
He looks very, very stupid.

00:26:54.128 --> 00:26:59.512
Now get him out of here, fast!

00:26:59.572 --> 00:27:12.638
Chapter 5 A Bad Day at the Gallery He got the painting into the men's room and started to wash it.

00:27:12.698 --> 00:27:19.904
There was no blue ink now, but where was Mrs Whistler's face?

00:27:19.964 --> 00:27:24.528
It was a long, difficult weekend for David.

00:27:24.588 --> 00:27:29.718
Then Monday arrived, the big day at the Grierson Gallery.

00:27:29.778 --> 00:27:37.450
In the car, on the way to the gallery, David said to Mr. Bean, Whistler's mother is arriving today.

00:27:37.510 --> 00:27:41.812
There are going to be a lot of important people at the gallery.

00:27:41.873 --> 00:27:46.396
When Mr. Bean didn't answer, David looked at him.

00:27:46.456 --> 00:27:48.287
Oh, no.

00:27:48.347 --> 00:27:52.339
Mr. Bean had a cigarette lighter up his nose.

00:27:52.400 --> 00:27:58.354
Please, Dr. Bean, please, don't do anything dangerous today.

00:27:58.414 --> 00:28:00.808
Please, David said.

00:28:00.868 --> 00:28:04.464
he really didn't want to lose his job.

00:28:04.524 --> 00:28:09.388
David and Mr. Bean walked into a big room in the gallery.

00:28:09.448 --> 00:28:13.661
There, at the end of the room, was Whistler's mother.

00:28:13.721 --> 00:28:17.514
Wonderful, said David, when he saw the painting.

00:28:17.574 --> 00:28:20.906
Mr. Grisson was there and smiled at him.

00:28:20.966 --> 00:28:24.269
Yes, it's very beautiful, he said.

00:28:24.329 --> 00:28:27.050
A really great work of art.

00:28:27.110 --> 00:28:29.623
Now, follow me, everybody.

00:28:29.683 --> 00:28:31.922
We've got to plan the day.

00:28:31.982 --> 00:28:34.552
He turned to Mr. Bean.

00:28:34.612 --> 00:28:37.324
Ah, good morning, Dr. Bean.

00:28:37.384 --> 00:28:41.358
Would you like to stay here and look after the painting?

00:28:41.418 --> 00:28:43.970
Ah, yes.

00:28:44.030 --> 00:28:45.401
OK.

00:28:45.461 --> 00:28:46.986
Said Mr. Bean.

00:28:47.046 --> 00:28:54.196
Then everybody left, and Mr Bean was the only person in the room with the famous painting.

00:28:54.256 --> 00:28:56.368
He was bored.

00:28:56.428 --> 00:29:00.724
He didn't want to look after Whistler's stupid old mother.

00:29:00.784 --> 00:29:04.248
He started to walk slowly round the room.

00:29:04.308 --> 00:29:08.614
When he got near the painting, he looked at it carefully.

00:29:08.674 --> 00:29:18.812
This painting's dirty," he thought, with his face very near the painting, and then he sneezed all over the painting.

00:29:18.872 --> 00:29:20.664
Oh, dear!

00:29:20.724 --> 00:29:27.258
He quickly got his handkerchief out of his jacket and started to clean the painting.

00:29:27.318 --> 00:29:28.748
Argh!

00:29:28.808 --> 00:29:30.540
He shouted a minute later.

00:29:30.600 --> 00:29:31.740
Oh, no!

00:29:31.800 --> 00:29:33.862
How did that happen?

00:29:33.922 --> 00:29:38.558
There was now blue ink all over Mrs. Whistler's face.

00:29:38.618 --> 00:29:42.134
He looked at his handkerchief.

00:29:42.194 --> 00:29:45.908
There was wet ink on that too.

00:29:45.968 --> 00:29:47.639
My pen!

00:29:47.699 --> 00:29:51.231
He cried, and took out his pen from his jacket.

00:29:51.292 --> 00:29:54.094
There was ink everywhere.

00:29:54.154 --> 00:29:56.236
What could he do?

00:29:56.296 --> 00:30:00.810
He thought for a minute, then took the painting off the wall.

00:30:00.870 --> 00:30:04.532
But it was very heavy and fell onto the floor.

00:30:04.592 --> 00:30:08.370
Then, by mistake, Mr. Bean stood on it.

00:30:08.430 --> 00:30:09.855
Help!

00:30:09.915 --> 00:30:13.828
He thought, this is getting worse and worse.

00:30:13.888 --> 00:30:18.062
He opened the door and looked out of the room.

00:30:18.122 --> 00:30:20.063
There was nobody there.

00:30:20.123 --> 00:30:24.626
With great difficulty, he carried the painting out of the room.

00:30:24.686 --> 00:30:28.519
The toilet, he thought, water.

00:30:28.580 --> 00:30:33.614
He got the painting into the men's room and started to wash it.

00:30:33.674 --> 00:30:39.796
There was no blue ink now, but where was Mrs. Whistler's face?

00:30:39.856 --> 00:30:43.037
Mr. Bean went hot and cold.

00:30:43.097 --> 00:30:45.838
Then he had an idea.

00:30:45.898 --> 00:30:49.479
The meeting finished, and David left the room.

00:30:49.539 --> 00:30:51.540
Right, he thought.

00:30:51.600 --> 00:30:56.831
Now I'll get Dr. Bean and have another look at our beautiful painting.

00:30:56.891 --> 00:31:01.730
But when he arrived at the room, he couldn't open the door.

00:31:01.790 --> 00:31:04.120
"'Dr. Bean,' he shouted.

00:31:04.140 --> 00:31:06.912
"'There's a problem with the door.

00:31:06.972 --> 00:31:09.604
Can you open it, please?'

00:31:09.664 --> 00:31:14.028
After a long time, Mr. Bean opened the door.

00:31:14.088 --> 00:31:16.390
David looked at him.

00:31:16.450 --> 00:31:18.752
Mr. Bean's face was grey.

00:31:18.772 --> 00:31:21.104
"'What's wrong?'

00:31:21.164 --> 00:31:22.404
he asked.

00:31:22.464 --> 00:31:24.886
"'I'm?'

00:31:24.946 --> 00:31:25.937
answered Mr. Bean.

00:31:25.957 --> 00:31:27.198
"'What?

00:31:27.258 --> 00:31:28.009
What?'

00:31:28.069 --> 00:31:29.420
cried David.

00:31:29.480 --> 00:31:32.498
Mr. Bean looked very afraid.

00:31:32.558 --> 00:31:36.798
It's um, it's the painting.

00:31:36.858 --> 00:31:38.430
He said quietly.

00:31:38.490 --> 00:31:41.092
Where is it, shouted David?

00:31:41.152 --> 00:31:43.124
Um, here.

00:31:43.184 --> 00:31:44.524
Said Mr Bean.

00:31:44.584 --> 00:31:46.796
He showed David the painting.

00:31:46.856 --> 00:31:52.412
I heard a little accident, but I think it's okay now.

00:31:52.472 --> 00:31:54.784
I painted a face on her.

00:31:54.844 --> 00:31:56.664
Do you like it?

00:31:56.724 --> 00:32:00.178
David looked at the painting with wide eyes.

00:32:00.238 --> 00:32:02.683
He felt sick.

00:32:02.743 --> 00:32:05.118
Oh no, he cried.

00:32:05.178 --> 00:32:07.488
No, no, no.

00:32:07.548 --> 00:32:12.720
What are we going to do now?

00:32:12.780 --> 00:32:26.033
Chapter 6 A Good Night's Work He put the bag on his back and jumped onto Kevin's bicycle.

00:32:26.093 --> 00:32:32.170
Then he rode quickly out of the garage, into the dark.

00:32:32.230 --> 00:32:35.878
It was midnight in the Langley's house.

00:32:35.938 --> 00:32:38.949
Allison and the children were home again.

00:32:39.009 --> 00:32:46.263
They didn't want to be in the same house as the strange Dr. Bean, but the children had to go to school.

00:32:46.323 --> 00:32:49.114
David was asleep in the sitting room.

00:32:49.174 --> 00:32:54.528
Allison was very angry with him and didn't want him in the bedroom.

00:32:54.588 --> 00:32:57.569
Mr. Bean couldn't sleep.

00:32:57.629 --> 00:33:00.164
He was very unhappy.

00:33:00.224 --> 00:33:02.380
He sat in the kitchen.

00:33:02.440 --> 00:33:04.712
He thought and thought.

00:33:04.772 --> 00:33:08.154
David will lose his job now.

00:33:08.214 --> 00:33:10.175
He thought sadly.

00:33:10.235 --> 00:33:14.308
At one o'clock, Kevin walked into the kitchen.

00:33:14.368 --> 00:33:16.068
He looked sleepy.

00:33:16.128 --> 00:33:17.880
Hi, Beanie.

00:33:17.940 --> 00:33:20.302
Oh, hello, Kevin.

00:33:20.362 --> 00:33:22.684
Why aren't you in bed?

00:33:22.744 --> 00:33:24.785
I couldn't sleep.

00:33:24.845 --> 00:33:29.797
I can't stop thinking about beautiful women with no clothes on.

00:33:29.857 --> 00:33:30.948
And you?

00:33:31.008 --> 00:33:32.438
said Kevin.

00:33:32.499 --> 00:33:36.640
I can't stop thinking about Whistler's mother.

00:33:36.700 --> 00:33:38.521
An said Mr Bean.

00:33:38.581 --> 00:33:42.242
Whistler's mother, boring.

00:33:42.302 --> 00:33:44.433
Come up to my room, Beanie.

00:33:44.494 --> 00:33:45.484
Said Kevin.

00:33:45.544 --> 00:33:49.436
I've got a great poster of Cindy Crawford up there.

00:33:49.496 --> 00:33:52.706
She's better than old Whistler's mother.

00:33:52.766 --> 00:33:56.607
Then he got a glass of milk and some chocolate cake.

00:33:56.668 --> 00:33:59.720
See you in the morning, Beanie.

00:33:59.780 --> 00:34:02.192
Kevin went back to bed.

00:34:02.252 --> 00:34:05.245
But Mr Bean sat at the kitchen table.

00:34:05.305 --> 00:34:10.320
He started thinking again, a poster of Cindy Crawford.

00:34:10.380 --> 00:34:13.842
Really, young people today.

00:34:13.902 --> 00:34:16.274
Wait a minute.

00:34:16.334 --> 00:34:17.518
He thought.

00:34:17.577 --> 00:34:25.116
Mr. Bean suddenly had an idea, another wonderful Mr. Bean idea.

00:34:25.176 --> 00:34:29.750
He stood up quickly and found a large bag in a cupboard.

00:34:29.809 --> 00:34:35.594
First he ran out of the kitchen and into the bathroom with the bag in his hands.

00:34:35.654 --> 00:34:44.300
Then he went quietly into Allison's bedroom, then into the kitchen again and then into the garage.

00:34:44.360 --> 00:34:47.906
After ten minutes the bag was very heavy.

00:34:47.966 --> 00:34:57.196
There was a hairdryer in it, a bicycle light, some eggs, some small bottles and a lot of other things.

00:34:57.256 --> 00:35:00.890
Next Mr Bean went into the sitting room.

00:35:00.950 --> 00:35:04.362
Now, where's David's card?

00:35:04.422 --> 00:35:10.288
He thought, I can't open the front door at the gallery without it.

00:35:10.348 --> 00:35:17.239
He found the card in David's jacket and put it in the bag with the other things.

00:35:17.299 --> 00:35:23.618
Then Mr Bean put on a black shirt, black jeans and a black hat.

00:35:23.678 --> 00:35:28.360
He put the bag on his back and jumped onto Kevin's bicycle.

00:35:28.420 --> 00:35:34.002
Then he rode quickly out of the garage into the dark.

00:35:34.062 --> 00:35:39.673
Fifteen minutes later Mr Bean arrived at the Grierson Gallery.

00:35:39.733 --> 00:35:45.528
He opened the front door with David's card and walked quietly into the building.

00:35:45.588 --> 00:35:47.961
It was two o'clock in the morning.

00:35:48.021 --> 00:35:49.552
Nobody saw him.

00:35:49.612 --> 00:35:53.014
Now, where's the gallery shop?

00:35:53.074 --> 00:35:54.274
He thought.

00:35:54.334 --> 00:35:57.126
He found the shop on the second floor.

00:35:57.187 --> 00:36:00.468
He carefully opened the door and went in.

00:36:00.528 --> 00:36:05.822
Great, he thought, when he saw a big poster of Whistler's mother.

00:36:05.882 --> 00:36:08.934
He put the poster in his bag.

00:36:08.994 --> 00:36:16.466
He then found the room with the famous painting, the painting of Whistler's mother with the funny face.

00:36:16.526 --> 00:36:19.537
He put his bag down on the floor.

00:36:19.597 --> 00:36:24.068
Right, let's start work, he thought.

00:36:24.128 --> 00:36:26.188
It was dark in the room.

00:36:26.248 --> 00:36:31.079
Mr. Bean took Kevin's bicycle light out of the bag and turned it on.

00:36:31.139 --> 00:36:34.580
Then he took out the poster of Whistler's mother.

00:36:34.640 --> 00:36:39.480
He looked at the poster and then at the famous painting on the wall.

00:36:39.540 --> 00:36:44.612
I've got to put a new surface on the poster," he thought.

00:36:44.672 --> 00:36:47.944
Then it'll be the same as the painting.

00:36:48.004 --> 00:36:54.239
He sat on the floor and slowly started painting a new surface onto the poster.

00:36:54.300 --> 00:37:00.014
He used the eggs from the Langley's kitchen and things from Alison's bottles.

00:37:00.074 --> 00:37:03.226
It was a long, difficult job.

00:37:03.286 --> 00:37:08.108
After two hours, Mr Bean stood up and looked at the poster.

00:37:08.168 --> 00:37:13.791
Hmm, that's better, he said, with a smile on his face.

00:37:13.851 --> 00:37:19.156
He took out the hairdryer from the bag and dried the new surface.

00:37:19.216 --> 00:37:23.400
Then he carefully took the famous painting off the wall.

00:37:23.460 --> 00:37:28.465
He put the poster with the new surface on the wall in the same place.

00:37:28.525 --> 00:37:33.188
Nobody will know it's only a poster, he thought.

00:37:33.248 --> 00:37:36.857
Then Mr Bean put everything back in his bag.

00:37:36.917 --> 00:37:42.570
He carried the bag and the old painting with the funny face out of the room.

00:37:42.630 --> 00:37:49.732
Out in the street, Mr Bean jumped onto Kevin's bicycle and rode back to the Langley's house.

00:37:49.792 --> 00:37:52.734
It was five o'clock in the morning.

00:37:52.794 --> 00:37:57.666
A good night's work, he thought, when he got into bed.

00:37:57.726 --> 00:38:03.740
David will be happy now.

00:38:03.800 --> 00:38:17.698
Chapter 7 Clever Dr. Bean All eyes were on the back of the painting behind Mr. Grierson.

00:38:17.758 --> 00:38:22.572
He slowly turned the painting round.

00:38:22.632 --> 00:38:29.036
The next morning, at breakfast time, David came slowly into the kitchen.

00:38:29.096 --> 00:38:32.538
His face looked old and tired.

00:38:32.598 --> 00:38:36.676
It's going to be a bad day today, he said.

00:38:36.736 --> 00:38:39.434
A very bad day.

00:38:39.494 --> 00:38:44.988
In the car, on the way to the gallery, Mr Bean tried to talk to David.

00:38:45.048 --> 00:38:48.320
He wanted to tell him about the painting.

00:38:48.380 --> 00:38:50.762
I'm David.

00:38:50.822 --> 00:38:54.114
Don't talk to me, I hate you.

00:38:54.174 --> 00:38:55.815
Answer David angrily.

00:38:55.876 --> 00:38:57.647
But David!

00:38:57.707 --> 00:38:58.928
Said Mr Bean.

00:38:58.988 --> 00:39:01.259
Quiet, shouted David.

00:39:01.320 --> 00:39:05.808
Don't say anything, or I'll kill you, okay?

00:39:05.868 --> 00:39:11.245
Outside the gallery, there were a lot of cars, people and cameras.

00:39:11.305 --> 00:39:15.757
Everybody wanted to see Whistler's famous painting of his mother.

00:39:15.818 --> 00:39:23.761
Inside, in the room with the painting, there were about a hundred important people from television and the newspapers.

00:39:23.821 --> 00:39:28.393
Nobody could see the painting, they could only see the back of it.

00:39:28.454 --> 00:39:31.896
David and Mr Bean walked into the room.

00:39:31.956 --> 00:39:35.727
David wanted to find Mr. Grierson as quickly as possible.

00:39:35.787 --> 00:39:39.618
He had to tell him about the accident with the painting.

00:39:39.678 --> 00:39:41.649
Oh, David!

00:39:41.709 --> 00:39:43.269
Said Mr. Grierson.

00:39:43.329 --> 00:39:46.810
And Dr. Bean, late again.

00:39:46.870 --> 00:39:48.521
Sorry, sir.

00:39:48.581 --> 00:39:50.272
A problem at home.

00:39:50.332 --> 00:39:53.042
Please, sir, I got to talk to you.

00:39:53.102 --> 00:39:55.575
Now, it's very important.

00:39:55.635 --> 00:39:57.338
Not now, David.

00:39:57.398 --> 00:39:58.828
Mr. Grierson answered.

00:39:58.888 --> 00:40:00.350
Everybody's waiting.

00:40:00.410 --> 00:40:03.071
We've got to show them the painting.

00:40:03.131 --> 00:40:05.522
But sir cried David.

00:40:05.582 --> 00:40:07.714
It's about the painting.

00:40:07.774 --> 00:40:10.755
But Mr. Grierson didn't listen.

00:40:10.815 --> 00:40:13.126
Mr. Bean looked at David.

00:40:13.186 --> 00:40:15.047
Ah, David.

00:40:15.107 --> 00:40:18.750
Bean, go away, David said.

00:40:18.810 --> 00:40:22.116
Mr. Grierson walked to the front of the room.

00:40:22.176 --> 00:40:24.912
Good morning, everybody," he said.

00:40:24.972 --> 00:40:30.534
This is a great day for America and for Whistler's mother.

00:40:30.594 --> 00:40:36.378
I won't say too much because I know you all want to see our famous painting.

00:40:36.438 --> 00:40:39.380
And here it is!

00:40:39.440 --> 00:40:42.022
David shot his eyes.

00:40:42.082 --> 00:40:45.471
I'm going to be sick, he thought.

00:40:45.531 --> 00:40:48.710
There wasn't a sound in the room.

00:40:48.770 --> 00:40:53.572
All eyes were on the back of the painting behind Mr. Grisson.

00:40:53.632 --> 00:40:57.614
He slowly turned the painting round.

00:40:57.674 --> 00:41:02.537
David stood at the back of the room next to Mr. Bean.

00:41:02.597 --> 00:41:04.748
He didn't understand.

00:41:04.808 --> 00:41:07.600
The painting looked wonderful.

00:41:07.660 --> 00:41:09.200
No blue ink.

00:41:09.260 --> 00:41:10.801
No funny face.

00:41:10.861 --> 00:41:13.227
There was nothing wrong with it.

00:41:13.287 --> 00:41:14.712
What?

00:41:14.772 --> 00:41:16.754
What did you do, Bean?

00:41:16.814 --> 00:41:18.164
He said quietly.

00:41:18.224 --> 00:41:19.885
You're wonderful.

00:41:19.945 --> 00:41:21.716
I love you.

00:41:21.776 --> 00:41:24.717
Easy, said Mr Bean.

00:41:24.778 --> 00:41:27.048
It's a poster.

00:41:27.109 --> 00:41:28.809
It's a what?

00:41:28.869 --> 00:41:30.860
But, but, but.

00:41:30.920 --> 00:41:32.091
Shh.

00:41:32.151 --> 00:41:34.022
Somebody will hear.

00:41:34.082 --> 00:41:37.068
But how did you do it?

00:41:37.128 --> 00:41:43.725
I came here in the middle of the night and took a poster from the shop, said Mr Bean.

00:41:43.785 --> 00:41:50.487
I painted a new surface on it with eggs and things, then I dried it with a hair dryer.

00:41:50.548 --> 00:41:52.358
What's the problem?

00:41:52.418 --> 00:41:54.929
But you can't.

00:41:54.989 --> 00:41:56.320
Shhh.

00:41:56.380 --> 00:41:58.210
Don't tell anybody.

00:41:58.270 --> 00:41:59.591
Loved Mr Bean.

00:41:59.651 --> 00:42:04.232
Nobody will know it's only a poster.

00:42:04.292 --> 00:42:08.433
Dr. Bean, are you ready?"

00:42:08.493 --> 00:42:10.244
asked Mr. Grayson.

00:42:10.304 --> 00:42:15.165
Mr. Bean didn't understand.—"Ready for what?"

00:42:15.225 --> 00:42:16.546
he asked.

00:42:16.606 --> 00:42:21.118
You're going to say something to these people, don't you remember?

00:42:21.178 --> 00:42:23.458
What shall I talk about?"

00:42:23.518 --> 00:42:27.910
About the painting, of course, laughed Mr. Grayson.

00:42:27.970 --> 00:42:31.444
This man was very strange.

00:42:31.504 --> 00:42:35.800
Yes, of course, said Mr. Beam.

00:42:35.860 --> 00:42:40.384
He went to the front of the room and smiled at the people and cameras.

00:42:40.444 --> 00:42:43.367
What did they want him to see?

00:42:43.427 --> 00:42:46.780
We're ready, said Mr. Grisson.

00:42:46.841 --> 00:42:52.266
You can start now.

00:42:52.326 --> 00:43:00.163
Thank you, and hello everybody.

00:43:00.183 --> 00:43:11.678
I'm Mr, sorry, Dr Bean, and I work at the National Gallery in London.

00:43:11.738 --> 00:43:16.740
I sit and look at paintings all day.

00:43:16.800 --> 00:43:18.701
Everybody liked that.

00:43:18.761 --> 00:43:20.522
They all smiled.

00:43:20.582 --> 00:43:23.892
He's very intelligent, they thought.

00:43:23.952 --> 00:43:30.794
Now, what can I say about this painting, said Mr Bean?

00:43:30.854 --> 00:43:34.206
And he looked at the famous Whistler's mother.

00:43:34.266 --> 00:43:41.839
First, it's very big.

00:43:41.899 --> 00:43:44.910
I like big paintings.

00:43:44.970 --> 00:43:46.661
Very clever.

00:43:46.721 --> 00:43:50.304
This man from London was really good.

00:43:50.364 --> 00:43:52.466
Next.

00:43:52.526 --> 00:43:55.998
And I'm nearly at the end now.

00:43:56.058 --> 00:43:59.850
Next is the big question.

00:43:59.910 --> 00:44:07.734
Why did this gallery pay thousands of dollars for this painting?

00:44:07.794 --> 00:44:10.926
Mr Bean looked at David.

00:44:10.986 --> 00:44:14.518
But David couldn't help him now.

00:44:14.578 --> 00:44:19.904
And the answer is...

00:44:19.964 --> 00:44:23.820
What is the answer?

00:44:23.880 --> 00:44:41.084
This painting is expensive because it's a picture of Whistler's mother and I know that families are very important.

00:44:41.144 --> 00:44:50.208
I know that because I'm staying with my best friend David and his lovely family.

00:44:50.268 --> 00:44:54.552
Whistler's mother wasn't a beautiful woman.

00:44:54.612 --> 00:44:56.504
Look at the painting.

00:44:56.564 --> 00:44:59.216
She's an ugly old thing.

00:44:59.276 --> 00:45:05.140
But she was his mother and he loved her.

00:45:05.201 --> 00:45:09.434
And I think that's wonderful.

00:45:09.494 --> 00:45:11.566
Everybody stood up.

00:45:11.626 --> 00:45:14.058
Thank you, Dr. Bean.

00:45:14.118 --> 00:45:15.938
Another photo, please.

00:45:15.998 --> 00:45:18.275
Look this way, Dr. Bean.

00:45:18.336 --> 00:45:24.413
Mr. Bean was famous, and David was very, very happy.

00:45:24.473 --> 00:45:30.204
But before David and Mr. Bean could leave the room, a policeman came in.

00:45:30.264 --> 00:45:31.795
Mr. Langley?

00:45:31.855 --> 00:45:35.466
He said to David, can I talk to you, sir?

00:45:35.526 --> 00:45:38.077
David looked at Mr. Bean.

00:45:38.137 --> 00:45:40.908
He was suddenly very afraid.

00:45:40.968 --> 00:45:44.920
It's okay, he said to the policeman quickly.

00:45:44.980 --> 00:45:47.686
I'll tell you everything.

00:45:47.746 --> 00:45:49.654
Everything?

00:45:49.714 --> 00:45:52.765
Yes, everything about the painting.

00:45:52.825 --> 00:45:54.156
What painting?

00:45:54.216 --> 00:45:57.467
I don't want to talk about a painting, said the policeman.

00:45:57.527 --> 00:45:59.418
I'm sorry, Mr. Langley.

00:45:59.478 --> 00:46:00.858
It's your daughter.

00:46:00.918 --> 00:46:02.569
She's in hospital.

00:46:02.629 --> 00:46:06.631
A road accident, sir.

00:46:06.691 --> 00:46:10.292
Chapter eight.

00:46:10.352 --> 00:46:12.970
At the hospital.

00:46:13.031 --> 00:46:17.212
He really wanted that sweet.

00:46:17.272 --> 00:46:22.428
Slowly, he put his hand into the man's stomach.

00:46:22.488 --> 00:46:27.154
He found the sweet and took it out.

00:46:27.214 --> 00:46:30.480
The hospital was very busy.

00:46:30.540 --> 00:46:34.346
David and Mr. Bean ran quickly to the front desk.

00:46:34.406 --> 00:46:36.826
Excuse me, David said.

00:46:36.886 --> 00:46:39.628
Can you tell me my daughter's room number?

00:46:39.688 --> 00:46:45.510
Jennifer Langley, she came in at about one o'clock, a road accident.

00:46:45.571 --> 00:46:47.712
One minute, sir.

00:46:47.772 --> 00:46:49.792
Said the woman at the desk.

00:46:49.852 --> 00:46:53.812
Ah, yes, she's in room 106.

00:46:53.872 --> 00:46:56.691
David ran up the stairs.

00:46:56.751 --> 00:46:58.512
Mr Bean followed him.

00:46:58.572 --> 00:47:01.002
No Bean, shouted David.

00:47:01.062 --> 00:47:04.473
You stay there and do nothing, nothing.

00:47:04.533 --> 00:47:07.223
Then nothing can go wrong.

00:47:07.283 --> 00:47:09.694
Mr Bean understood.

00:47:09.754 --> 00:47:12.204
He watched David leave.

00:47:12.264 --> 00:47:14.224
He felt very sad.

00:47:14.284 --> 00:47:16.195
He wanted to help.

00:47:16.255 --> 00:47:19.196
And he wanted a family too.

00:47:19.256 --> 00:47:22.812
David found room 106 and went in.

00:47:22.872 --> 00:47:27.679
Jennifer was in bed, and Alison was on a chair next to her.

00:47:27.740 --> 00:47:30.510
Ali, how is she?

00:47:30.570 --> 00:47:34.862
Oh, David, I don't know, cried Alison.

00:47:34.922 --> 00:47:37.672
I'm waiting for the doctor.

00:47:37.732 --> 00:47:41.734
Mr. Bean sat and waited for David.

00:47:41.794 --> 00:47:46.956
After some time, he felt bored and started to walk around the hospital.

00:47:47.016 --> 00:47:51.056
A doctor suddenly ran out of a room and saw Mr. Bean.

00:47:51.116 --> 00:47:52.426
Who are you?

00:47:52.486 --> 00:47:53.578
He asked.

00:47:53.638 --> 00:47:54.729
Me.

00:47:54.789 --> 00:47:56.941
I'm Dr. Bean.

00:47:57.001 --> 00:47:57.992
Good.

00:47:58.052 --> 00:47:59.614
I'm Dr. Jacobson.

00:47:59.674 --> 00:48:02.266
I want some help, Dr. Come with me.

00:48:02.326 --> 00:48:03.818
Oh, no.

00:48:03.878 --> 00:48:06.460
Mr. Bean wasn't really a doctor.

00:48:06.520 --> 00:48:11.922
He was only Dr. Bean at the Grierson Gallery, not in a hospital.

00:48:11.982 --> 00:48:13.452
I'm...

00:48:13.512 --> 00:48:14.692
I'm...

00:48:14.712 --> 00:48:16.744
I'm really Mr. Bean.

00:48:16.804 --> 00:48:18.174
Not Doctor.

00:48:18.234 --> 00:48:21.556
He said that Dr. Jacobson was too busy.

00:48:21.616 --> 00:48:23.438
He didn't hear him.

00:48:23.498 --> 00:48:27.719
Mr. Bean followed Dr. Jacobson into an operating room.

00:48:27.780 --> 00:48:29.881
Okay, listen everybody.

00:48:29.941 --> 00:48:31.662
This is Dr. Bean.

00:48:31.722 --> 00:48:34.934
Doctor, this man's got a bullet in his stomach.

00:48:34.994 --> 00:48:36.314
It's bad.

00:48:36.374 --> 00:48:41.090
I've got another operation in room four, but I'll see you later.

00:48:41.150 --> 00:48:47.505
Dr. Jacobson ran out of the operating room, and everybody looked at Dr. Bean.

00:48:47.565 --> 00:48:52.747
Here, Dr. Put these clothes on, somebody said.

00:48:52.807 --> 00:48:55.358
Dr. this man's dying.

00:48:55.418 --> 00:49:00.929
Do something fast, another person said.

00:49:00.990 --> 00:49:04.941
Mr. Bean didn't answer.

00:49:05.001 --> 00:49:08.492
Shall I make the first cut, Dr. Bean?

00:49:08.553 --> 00:49:10.844
asked a very young doctor.

00:49:10.904 --> 00:49:13.725
Okay, said Mr Bean.

00:49:13.785 --> 00:49:16.916
He felt very, very afraid.

00:49:16.976 --> 00:49:21.058
The young doctor started to cut open the man's stomach.

00:49:21.118 --> 00:49:25.270
Mr Bean watched and felt very sick.

00:49:25.330 --> 00:49:29.972
Suddenly, somebody outside shouted, quick!

00:49:30.032 --> 00:49:30.862
Help!

00:49:30.922 --> 00:49:32.413
We're losing her!

00:49:32.473 --> 00:49:33.766
Help!

00:49:33.826 --> 00:49:41.754
Everybody in the operating room ran out, and Mr. Bean was the only person in the room again.

00:49:41.814 --> 00:49:46.616
He waited for the other people, but nobody came back.

00:49:46.676 --> 00:49:50.670
After some time he took out a packet of sweets.

00:49:50.730 --> 00:49:55.572
He threw a sweet up into the air and tried to catch it in his mouth.

00:49:55.632 --> 00:50:00.942
But the sweet fell into the stomach of the man on the operating table.

00:50:01.002 --> 00:50:03.600
Mr. Bean looked down.

00:50:03.660 --> 00:50:06.782
He really wanted that sweet.

00:50:06.842 --> 00:50:11.346
Slowly he put his hand into the man's stomach.

00:50:11.406 --> 00:50:15.208
He found the sweet and took it out.

00:50:15.268 --> 00:50:19.902
But it wasn't his sweet, it was the bullet.

00:50:19.962 --> 00:50:24.695
Mr. Bean was hungry, but he couldn't eat a bullet.

00:50:24.755 --> 00:50:30.605
He quickly put it back into the man's stomach and then found his sweet.

00:50:30.665 --> 00:50:34.972
He washed it and put it into his mouth.

00:50:35.032 --> 00:50:37.462
Lovely.

00:50:37.522 --> 00:50:42.253
A minute later, everybody ran back into the operating room.

00:50:42.313 --> 00:50:47.064
Okay, let's find that bullet, said the young doctor.

00:50:47.124 --> 00:50:50.745
He looked in the man's stomach, but he couldn't see it.

00:50:50.805 --> 00:50:53.025
I can't see anything.

00:50:53.085 --> 00:50:55.045
Where is that bullet?

00:50:55.105 --> 00:50:58.824
We'll have to find it, or he's a dead man.

00:50:58.884 --> 00:51:01.384
Mr Bean watched him.

00:51:01.444 --> 00:51:07.328
He thought for a minute, and then said, no problem here.

00:51:07.388 --> 00:51:08.548
I'll do it.

00:51:08.609 --> 00:51:11.870
He carefully put his hands into the man's stomach.

00:51:11.930 --> 00:51:16.124
Everybody shouted, stop, you can't do that.

00:51:16.184 --> 00:51:19.606
Take your hands out, it's too dangerous.

00:51:19.666 --> 00:51:22.268
Mr Bean didn't listen.

00:51:22.328 --> 00:51:26.491
He took his hands out of the man's stomach and smiled.

00:51:26.552 --> 00:51:29.110
He showed them the bullet.

00:51:29.170 --> 00:51:30.828
What?

00:51:30.888 --> 00:51:34.150
I don't understand, cried the young doctor.

00:51:34.210 --> 00:51:38.072
Wonderful, wonderful, they all shouted.

00:51:38.132 --> 00:51:43.815
Dr. Bean's the cleverest doctor in the world.

00:51:43.875 --> 00:51:51.639
Chapter 9 We love you, Mr. Bean.

00:51:51.699 --> 00:51:56.302
Yes, it's me, he said.

00:51:56.362 --> 00:51:59.891
And I'd like to stay with you in Los Angeles.

00:51:59.952 --> 00:52:02.822
for another week.

00:52:02.882 --> 00:52:09.654
Five minutes later, Mr Bean walked out of the operating room in his blue doctor's clothes.

00:52:09.714 --> 00:52:13.806
Phew, I'd like a cup of coffee, he thought.

00:52:13.866 --> 00:52:18.398
Suddenly somebody behind him shouted, Doctor, Doctor!

00:52:18.458 --> 00:52:19.859
Oh no!

00:52:19.919 --> 00:52:22.580
thought Mr Bean, not again.

00:52:22.640 --> 00:52:26.263
He turned round, and there was David.

00:52:26.323 --> 00:52:28.646
Doctor, come quickly.

00:52:28.706 --> 00:52:29.967
It's my daughter.

00:52:30.027 --> 00:52:31.749
She's in room 106.

00:52:31.809 --> 00:52:33.070
Quick!"

00:52:33.130 --> 00:52:35.593
Mr. Bean couldn't say no.

00:52:35.653 --> 00:52:38.286
He had to go and see Jennifer.

00:52:38.346 --> 00:52:40.058
Oh, Doctor!

00:52:40.118 --> 00:52:43.842
cried Allison when she saw Mr. Bean in his doctor's clothes.

00:52:43.902 --> 00:52:44.813
Quick!

00:52:44.873 --> 00:52:46.725
Do something!

00:52:46.785 --> 00:52:51.045
Mr. Bean looked at Jennifer on the bed.

00:52:51.105 --> 00:52:58.967
Mr. and Mrs. He started to say, Langley said David and Alison.

00:52:59.028 --> 00:53:12.778
Yes, Mr. and Mrs. Langley, your daughter is going to be fine, but I'd like to see her without you here.

00:53:12.838 --> 00:53:17.480
Of course, Doctor, they said, and left quickly.

00:53:17.540 --> 00:53:22.372
Mr. Bean was the only person in the room, again.

00:53:22.432 --> 00:53:25.474
Everything was very quiet.

00:53:25.534 --> 00:53:27.916
Not a sound.

00:53:27.976 --> 00:53:31.169
Mr. Bean slowly went to Jennifer's bed.

00:53:31.189 --> 00:53:34.201
A Jennifer?

00:53:34.262 --> 00:53:35.452
He said.

00:53:35.512 --> 00:53:38.436
Wake up!

00:53:38.496 --> 00:53:40.728
Wake up!

00:53:40.788 --> 00:53:43.179
Wake up!

00:53:43.239 --> 00:53:46.274
Jennifer didn't open her eyes.

00:53:46.334 --> 00:53:50.940
Mr. Bean sat on the bed and put his face near Jennifer's.

00:53:51.000 --> 00:53:54.032
Then he started making funny faces.

00:53:54.092 --> 00:53:55.953
Baaah!

00:53:56.013 --> 00:53:57.384
He shouted.

00:53:57.444 --> 00:53:58.915
Argh!

00:53:58.975 --> 00:54:01.456
Jennifer didn't move.

00:54:01.516 --> 00:54:04.698
Next, Mr. Bean hit her.

00:54:04.758 --> 00:54:06.810
Nothing happened.

00:54:06.870 --> 00:54:10.882
He climbed onto her bed and looked down at her.

00:54:10.942 --> 00:54:14.484
Then he jumped on top of her, hard.

00:54:14.544 --> 00:54:16.818
And Jennifer woke up.

00:54:16.878 --> 00:54:17.982
Dad!

00:54:18.042 --> 00:54:18.763
Mom!

00:54:18.823 --> 00:54:19.474
Help!"

00:54:19.534 --> 00:54:20.794
she shouted.

00:54:20.854 --> 00:54:24.128
Mr. Bean got off the bed quickly.

00:54:24.188 --> 00:54:27.750
Outside, David and Alison heard their daughter.

00:54:27.810 --> 00:54:30.972
They ran into the room as fast as they could.

00:54:31.033 --> 00:54:32.334
Jennifer!

00:54:32.394 --> 00:54:33.234
cried Alison.

00:54:33.294 --> 00:54:34.585
You're okay.

00:54:34.646 --> 00:54:36.327
What happened, Mom?

00:54:36.387 --> 00:54:37.628
Jennifer asked.

00:54:37.688 --> 00:54:39.950
Her eyes were wide open now.

00:54:40.010 --> 00:54:42.332
You had an accident, dear.

00:54:42.392 --> 00:54:45.860
But everything's going to be okay now.

00:54:45.920 --> 00:54:51.026
Mr. Bean watched the happy family, then walked to the door.

00:54:51.086 --> 00:54:52.927
David looked round.

00:54:52.947 --> 00:54:58.698
"'Doctor, don't go,' he said to Mr. Bean, with a smile on his face.

00:54:58.758 --> 00:55:01.059
How are little girls okay?

00:55:01.119 --> 00:55:03.069
And we want to thank you, Doctor.'

00:55:03.089 --> 00:55:07.530
"'Yes, Doctor, thank you a thousand times,' said Alison.

00:55:07.550 --> 00:55:10.271
"'What can we do for you now?

00:55:10.331 --> 00:55:11.771
We want to thank you.

00:55:11.831 --> 00:55:14.814
We'll do anything, anything.'

00:55:14.875 --> 00:55:17.608
Mr. Bean thought for a minute.

00:55:17.668 --> 00:55:20.739
Then he took off his doctor's clothes.

00:55:20.800 --> 00:55:23.961
It's Mr. Bean, they shouted.

00:55:24.021 --> 00:55:27.072
Yes, it's me, he said.

00:55:27.132 --> 00:55:33.045
And I'd like to stay with you in Los Angeles for another week.

00:55:33.106 --> 00:55:37.578
Another week with this strange Englishman.

00:55:37.638 --> 00:55:40.740
Strange but wonderful too.

00:55:40.800 --> 00:55:44.199
Yes, Mr. Bean was a friend now.

00:55:44.260 --> 00:55:47.220
Of course, they all shouted.

00:55:47.280 --> 00:55:52.013
We love you, Mr. Bean.

00:55:52.073 --> 00:55:59.218
Chapter 10 It's a poster.

00:55:59.278 --> 00:56:03.010
Mr. Bean got into bed.

00:56:03.071 --> 00:56:10.699
Before he went to sleep, he looked up at the wall opposite his bed and smiled.

00:56:10.760 --> 00:56:15.046
Mr Bean had a great week in Los Angeles.

00:56:15.106 --> 00:56:18.269
There were only one or two accidents.

00:56:18.329 --> 00:56:23.693
The time went quickly, and then it was the end of his holiday in America.

00:56:23.753 --> 00:56:31.540
On his last day with the Langleys, they had a big party, and Mr Bean took more photos of everybody.

00:56:31.600 --> 00:56:34.302
Then they had to say goodbye.

00:56:34.362 --> 00:56:39.664
Goodbye, dear Mr Bean, said Alison and the children outside the house.

00:56:39.724 --> 00:56:42.355
Please come and visit us again.

00:56:42.415 --> 00:56:44.928
Good-bye, everybody.

00:56:44.988 --> 00:56:49.091
Thank you very much for my lovely holiday.

00:56:49.151 --> 00:56:52.694
David drove Mr Bean to the airport.

00:56:52.754 --> 00:56:56.598
There were no policemen there with guns this time.

00:56:56.658 --> 00:57:02.398
Well, goodbye Beanie, said David, and put his arm round him.

00:57:02.458 --> 00:57:08.895
Have a good journey back to England and come back sometime in the future.

00:57:08.955 --> 00:57:13.687
David liked Mr Bean but he remembered the bad times too.

00:57:13.747 --> 00:57:16.048
Goodbye David.

00:57:16.108 --> 00:57:17.289
Said Mr Bean.

00:57:17.349 --> 00:57:20.130
Thank you for everything.

00:57:20.190 --> 00:57:23.362
Mr Bean turned and walked away.

00:57:23.422 --> 00:57:27.256
David watched him and then left the airport.

00:57:27.316 --> 00:57:30.711
Suddenly he felt somebody behind him.

00:57:30.771 --> 00:57:34.222
He turned round and there was Mr Bean.

00:57:34.282 --> 00:57:40.393
Mr Bean wanted to take one last photo and to put his arms round David too.

00:57:40.454 --> 00:57:43.944
Then he was ready to leave America.

00:57:44.004 --> 00:57:54.168
Three years later, Mr Bean sat in his little house in England and thought about his wonderful holiday in America.

00:57:54.228 --> 00:58:01.418
Before he went to bed, he looked at the photos of his good friends, the Langleys, on his sitting-room wall.

00:58:01.478 --> 00:58:03.300
He smiled.

00:58:03.360 --> 00:58:07.202
In Los Angeles, it was a beautiful afternoon.

00:58:07.263 --> 00:58:14.956
At the Grierson Gallery, David sat in the room with Whistler's mother and thought about his strange friend, Mr. Bean.

00:58:15.016 --> 00:58:18.870
He looked at the famous painting and laughed.

00:58:18.930 --> 00:58:23.724
Suddenly, his cup of coffee began to move across the table.

00:58:23.784 --> 00:58:27.016
Then the painting began to move too.

00:58:27.076 --> 00:58:28.757
Oh, no!

00:58:28.818 --> 00:58:30.308
cried David.

00:58:30.368 --> 00:58:33.310
Mr. Grierson ran into the room.

00:58:33.370 --> 00:58:35.691
The ground's moving, David!"

00:58:35.751 --> 00:58:36.631
he shouted.

00:58:36.691 --> 00:58:37.932
The paintings!

00:58:37.992 --> 00:58:41.404
Why are we going to do about the paintings?

00:58:41.464 --> 00:58:46.516
Before David could answer, Whistler's mother fell off the wall.

00:58:46.576 --> 00:58:50.217
Mr. Grierson looked at the painting on the floor.

00:58:50.278 --> 00:58:51.588
No!

00:58:51.648 --> 00:58:52.579
No!

00:58:52.639 --> 00:58:54.039
He suddenly cried out.

00:58:54.099 --> 00:58:54.780
Look!

00:58:54.840 --> 00:58:56.380
David, look!

00:58:56.440 --> 00:58:58.582
David looked down.

00:58:58.642 --> 00:59:01.854
On the back of the painting were the words.

00:59:01.915 --> 00:59:06.408
Whistler's mother, a Grierson Gallery poster.

00:59:06.468 --> 00:59:09.190
It's a poster, David!

00:59:09.250 --> 00:59:10.741
A poster!

00:59:10.801 --> 00:59:15.254
So, so where's the painting?

00:59:15.314 --> 00:59:19.906
In England, Mr Bean got into bed.

00:59:19.966 --> 00:59:26.110
Before he went to sleep, he looked up at the wall opposite his bed and smiled.

00:59:26.170 --> 00:59:28.342
Good night, old dear.

00:59:28.402 --> 00:59:31.736
He said, and turned off the light.

00:59:31.796 --> 00:59:34.573
What was on the wall?

00:59:34.633 --> 00:59:40.433
The famous painting, Whistler's mother, of course, with the funny face.

